<title>USA: FSA qualifies six muni bond issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies six muni bond issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said Monday it qualified for bond insurance the following six municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Wyoming, Mich., $655,000 general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Wyoming, Mich., $660,000 special assessment bonds.</p>
<p>--Wyoming, Mich., $3.9 million MTF debt.</p>
<p>--Grand Forks, N.D., $4.53 million refunding and improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Pennridge School District, Pa., $9.995 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Elkhorn, Wis., $4.525 million GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
